---
// Ladygraph is dark by construction, like the graph viewer it documents.
// Starlight's default provider reads a stored preference and the system one,
// and its light palette lives entirely under `[data-theme='light']`; pinning
// the attribute here is what keeps that palette from ever being selected.
//
// `updatePickers` stays defined and does nothing: Starlight's own scripts call
// it, and there is no picker to update because ThemeSelect is overridden too.
---

{/* Inlined, like the component it replaces, to avoid a flash of wrong theme. */}
<script is:inline>
  window.StarlightThemeProvider = {
    updatePickers() {},
  };
  document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "dark";
</script>
